@startuml AircraftManagement-SD-TopUtilizedModels
autonumber
title Top most utilised aircraft models — GET /api/aircraft-models/top-utilized?limit=5 (US204, contract B4b)
actor "Backoffice Operator / ATCC" as User
participant "aircraftmanagement-1\n: AircraftModelStatisticsController" as Ctrl
participant ": TopUtilizedModelsService" as Service
participant ": SearchAircraftsService" as Search
participant ": FlightRoutesClient" as FRC
participant "Flight Routes\n(replicas)" as FR

activate User
User -> Ctrl : GET /api/aircraft-models/top-utilized?limit=5
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Ctrl : 1 <= limit <= 20 (else 400)
Ctrl -> Service : topUtilized(5)
activate Service
Service -> Search : search(null, null, null)
Search --> Service : fleet of ALL replicas (registration → model)
Service -> FRC : minutesByAircraft()
FRC -> FR : GET /api/scheduled-flights/statistics/minutes-by-aircraft\n(JWT of the user forwarded)
FR --> FRC : 200 {"CS-TUA": 55, "CS-TUC": 140, ...}
FRC --> Service : MinutesByAircraft(minutes, partial)

Service -> Service : sum minutes per model (via the fleet)\ncount aircraft per model\ndrop models with 0 minutes
Service -> Service : sort by minutes desc (ties: model name)\nlimit(5)
Service --> Ctrl : Result(rows, partial)
deactivate Service
Ctrl --> User : 200 OK (List<ModelUtilizationDTO>)\n+ X-Partial-Response: true (only if partial)
deactivate Ctrl

note over User, FR
  Flight Routes only knows registrations, so the mapping registration → model is done here.
  "Most utilised" = flight time (contract Q5).
  FR accepts only ATCC on /api/scheduled-flights/**: a Backoffice token gets 403
  "Flight Routes rejected the request." until that rule changes (contract Q4).
end note
@enduml
